## Checker and digits

Natural forms that drop a source digit fail `numbers`. The checker compares to the Korean file. Restored the smallest form that still parses, and noted it here:

- 001 „das letzte Jahr“ drops Korean 최근 1년. Now „das letzte Jahr (1 Jahr)“ ×2.
- 002 „jeder Ruhezeitraum darf ein Jahr“ drops Korean 1회 beside 1년. Now „die Dauer von 1 Ruhezeitraum darf ein Jahr nicht überschreiten“ ×2. This does not restore „1 Mal“ („only once“).
- 008 „jedes vollendete Jahr“ and „je vollem Jahr ein Monatsbetrag“ („ein Monatsbetrag“ is not in the German lexicon). Now „jedes vollendete Jahr (1 Jahr)“ ×2 and „pro 1 Jahr 1 Monatsbetrag“ ×2.
- 010 deleting „(bis zum 1-fachen)“ drops the 1 in 1배. Now „(1-fach)“, which is the German word, not the calque „1-fachen“.
- 018 „jeder Gesellschafter eine Stimme“ drops 1인 and 1표 („eine Stimme“ is not in the lexicon). Now „hat 1 Gesellschafter 1 Stimme“.

010 still WARNs an extra 2020 (Gregorian year already in the judgment gloss). The file PASSes. That warning was not introduced as a new digit in running text beyond the existing year gloss.

## Reviewer points not followed

- de-a 15 and the U+200B „pad“ are not a German-only defect. The counts match the Korean source. Treating them as disposable blank lines would fail the checker.
- de-b 32. The three short blocks are the English structure, not a German blog merge waiting to happen.
- R8 „write parent company, not the mother“. German legal usage for 母公司 is Muttergesellschaft, and „die Mutter“ in 018 is that short form. Replacing it with a calque of „parent company“ would be less native. Left as it is.
- 007 „Personenstandsregister“ glosses 戶政機關 and the 戶籍法 filing regime. Part a called 007 native professional and did not flag it. The 016 fix is limited to 戶籍. 007 Namensleihe (借名登記) is name-borrowing of title, not 借牌, so it was not swept with the 017 licence-lending fix.
- de-a 24’s request to delete the Schwierigkeit row. The English source has the same row. Deleting it changes the table. The cells were softened instead.

